    <h1>Five rewrites of<br>a 1-bit matmul</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Q1_0 stores every weight as a single bit: <b>+1 or -1</b>. The multiply is not real work,
      so the whole cost of the kernel is how the bits are laid out and how many lanes of the
      vector unit are busy. Changing the layout four times and the instruction once took one
      matmul node from <b>4.48M cycles to 363K</b>, with bit-identical results.
    </p>

